10","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"f4518f0eeb0aa31ccd01f4d7297518fa4bf20ef00226bf21704a6dc8d333fdc1","compact":"d14d0c7ff69eac99a85f4f4558136768da8584608eeb3d1e7105d303fe683648","nasal":"f9a95416c2f7611c12b784d6b196c7cdec2c3d841e5a17510d099493f3401679"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-3-11","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":3,"verse":11,"english":"(At those gates) are powerful and large arms, stones, and engines, whereby a hostile host approaching, is opposed.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.833,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-3-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6003011","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d601ffaf00d94315888cdc77facb4fde095b67beadf0714e900969b20af30bae","compact":"16ab0a5f018acd4055370a6696208fe9f223065e3a982cfb21c7c88d91c6cd02","nasal":"1c5fa055502f61f7128d39375e3c48a30d20f7b7a155235201975fcae2d8c9c2"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-3-12","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":3,"verse":12,"english":"At the entrances are arrayed and set in order by bands of heroic Rākşasas, hundreds of dreadful sharp iron sataghnis.* *A kind of fire-arms, or ancient Hindu rocket; or a stone set round with sharp iron spikes. According to Rāmānuja, a sort of mace about two yards in length, with spikes.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.873,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-3-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6003012","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"4ae3758beba520b96d4f9f92b91388c0dad61fc6caaf72e1e990c839dfda37a5","compact":"66fd5037cd36ad70103a255650cf4769139515017e862625f6aed4e12fb99c67","nasal":"66fd5037cd36ad70103a255650cf4769139515017e862625f6aed4e12fb99c67"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-3-13","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":3,"verse":13,"english":"She has a mighty impassable golden wall, having its side 